@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] observability-independent-authority
This library MUST emit only reviewed observability data and MUST NOT acquire
application, database, VM, guest or control-protocol authority. Exporter failure
MUST NOT change application work results, locks, receipts or recovery decisions.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] observability-reviewed-data
Span names and attributes MUST have a reviewed schema. Credentials, command
arguments, URLs, terminal or disk bytes, payloads and exception messages MUST NOT
reach spans, exporters or diagnostics. Exporter error bodies MUST remain private.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] observability-custody-ack
A successful export MUST mean its spans reached the independent spool's
reviewed SQLite FULL WAL fsync boundary. Queue admission inside the SDK MUST NOT be
described as durable.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:capacity] observability-bounded-producers
Routine emission MUST use a bounded queue and fail open under unavailable or
full observability storage. No observer I/O MAY occur inside native ownership,
fork, pre-exec, signal, disk-stream or terminal-byte critical regions.
